{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rt8PqP8s1K9HUKgeHUhe2B","type":"tool_result","content":"1122\t**1. B.**\n1123\t\n1124\tmetrics-server is a \"Cluster addon component\" and the Metrics API requires \"an API extension server that provides the Metrics API.\" [source: k8s-docs-resource-metrics-pipeline-2026-08-31] Without it, there is no endpoint to answer the request, which is why the error is about the resource, not about any particular node.\n1125\t\n1126\t- **A is wrong.** This is not a permissions problem, and healthy nodes reporting normally would not produce it.\n1127\t- **C is wrong.** `kubectl top` is current and unremoved.\n1128\t- **D is wrong.** The question stipulates every node is `Ready` and every workload is healthy, and in any case memory pressure would not manifest as a missing API.\n1129\t\n1130\t**2. C.** *[retrieval: ch8]*\n1131\t\n1132\t\"`kubelet` may be up to three minor versions older than `kube-apiserver`,\" and the documented example is exactly this: \"`kube-apiserver` is at **1.37**; `kubelet` is supported at **1.37**, **1.36**, **1.35**, and **1.34**.\" [source: k8s-version-skew-policy-2026-08-31]\n1133\t\n1134\tWait — that example lists 1.34 as the oldest, not 1.33. Count carefully: three minor versions older than 1.37 is 1.34. **1.33 is four behind and is not supported.**\n1135\t\n1136\tSo the correct answer is **B**, not C.\n1137\t\n1138\t- **B is correct** — the rule is \"up to three minor versions older,\" 1.34 is the floor against a 1.37 API server, and 1.33 falls outside it.\n1139\t- **C is wrong** in its arithmetic: 1.33 is four minors behind 1.37, not three. This distractor exists because the off-by-one is the actual error people make.\n1140\t- **A is wrong** — there is a bound, and it is three.\n1141\t- **D is wrong** — exact matching is not required; that is the whole point of the skew window, which exists so that clusters can be upgraded a component at a time.\n1142\t\n1143\t<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: the answer text above works through a self-correction mid-answer, which is not the house form for an answer key. Revision stage: rewrite as a clean answer keyed to B, and rebuild option C's wording so the off-by-one is still the trap without the key having to walk into it. The underlying fact and the source citation are correct as given. -->"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed863541-8a1f-4f92-a038-f7da00387088","uuid":"b2aafab0-0e43-4392-9ca9-bf328ef07e73","timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:18:04.133Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-13\\draft-v1.md","content":"**1. B.**\n\nmetrics-server is a \"Cluster addon component\" and the Metrics API requires \"an API extension server that provides the Metrics API.\" [source: k8s-docs-resource-metrics-pipeline-2026-08-31] Without it, there is no endpoint to answer the request, which is why the error is about the resource, not about any particular node.\n\n- **A is wrong.** This is not a permissions problem, and healthy nodes reporting normally would not produce it.\n- **C is wrong.** `kubectl top` is current and unremoved.\n- **D is wrong.** The question stipulates every node is `Ready` and every workload is healthy, and in any case memory pressure would not manifest as a missing API.\n\n**2. C.** *[retrieval: ch8]*\n\n\"`kubelet` may be up to three minor versions older than `kube-apiserver`,\" and the documented example is exactly this: \"`kube-apiserver` is at **1.37**; `kubelet` is supported at **1.37**, **1.36**, **1.35**, and **1.34**.\" [source: k8s-version-skew-policy-2026-08-31]\n\nWait — that example lists 1.34 as the oldest, not 1.33. Count carefully: three minor versions older than 1.37 is 1.34. **1.33 is four behind and is not supported.**\n\nSo the correct answer is **B**, not C.\n\n- **B is correct** — the rule is \"up to three minor versions older,\" 1.34 is the floor against a 1.37 API server, and 1.33 falls outside it.\n- **C is wrong** in its arithmetic: 1.33 is four minors behind 1.37, not three. This distractor exists because the off-by-one is the actual error people make.\n- **A is wrong** — there is a bound, and it is three.\n- **D is wrong** — exact matching is not required; that is the whole point of the skew window, which exists so that clusters can be upgraded a component at a time.\n\n<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: the answer text above works through a self-correction mid-answer, which is not the house form for an answer key. Revision stage: rewrite as a clean answer keyed to B, and rebuild option C's wording so the off-by-one is still the trap without the key having to walk into it. The underlying fact and the source citation are correct as given. -->","numLines":22,"startLine":1122,"totalLines":1533}}}
